# menudesk.ai — marketing site
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Both values below are also set on Vercel for
# Production, Preview and Development; .env.local only covers local runs.
#
# These are destinations, not secrets. Nothing here grants access to anything,
# which is why this file can live in the repo — unlike .env.local, which is
# ignored.

# Where the funnel actually runs. next.config.mjs rewrites /scan, /r, /s,
# /upgrade, /precise and the funnel's /api routes to this origin, so that
# menudesk.ai serves the app on one domain (Bible Addendum v2.1 §18) instead of
# sending owners to a second hostname mid-decision.
#
# Required. A production build FAILS without it rather than shipping a site
# whose /scan quietly 404s.
MENUDESK_APP_ORIGIN=https://menudesk-app.vercel.app

# Where every call to action points. One variable so the destination can move
# without a code change: point it at the LINE OA during the concierge phase,
# and at /scan once the funnel is live.
#
# Optional — defaults to /scan. NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined at BUILD time, so
# changing it on Vercel does nothing until the next deployment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SCAN_URL=/scan
